{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a2096"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge belief/mythology","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/belief__mythology.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",495],["+"," The creature itself is far older than Greece. In Egypt a sphinx was a lion with the head of a king, wingless and male, and the Great Sphinx of Giza, carved out of the bedrock in the 4th Dynasty around 2600 BC, is a recumbent lion with a human face – the oldest monumental sculpture in the country."],["=",189],["-","Cerberus,"],["+","Cerberus"],["=",1],["-","the"],["+","is"],["=",1],["+","a dog – a monstrous "],["=",12],["+","whom Hesiod's \"Theogony\" already named around 700 BC. He "],["=",350],["-","woman's"],["+","human"],["=",3],["+","(a woman's in Greece) "],["=",79]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",481],["+"," Das Wesen selbst ist viel älter als Griechenland. In Ägypten war eine Sphinx ein Löwe mit dem Kopf eines Königs, ohne Flügel und männlich, und die Große Sphinx von Gizeh, in der 4. Dynastie um 2600 v. Chr. aus dem anstehenden Fels gehauen, ist ein liegender Löwe mit Menschengesicht – die älteste Monumentalskulptur des Landes."],["=",183],["-","Zerberus),"],["+","Zerberus)"],["=",1],["-","der"],["+","ist"],["=",1],["-","dreiköpfige"],["+","ein"],["=",3],["+","– ein ungeheurer dreiköpfiger Höllenhund "],["=",4],["+","den schon Hesiods „Theogonie“ um 700 v. Chr. nennt. Er "],["=",326],["-","Frauenkopf"],["+","Menschenkopf"],["=",1],["+","(in Griechenland einem Frauenkopf) "],["=",81]]}]},
